# One step writes a note, a later one reads it in `with open(..) as f` and returns `f.read()`: `f` is bound to what
# `open` gives, and what is read goes back to `run`, which prints it. The note stands between the two steps.

route withopen.run
step run/save
step run/load
line entry > run call
line run/save > File(data/note.txt) own
line File(data/note.txt) > run/load own
line run/load > run back                       # the note, a str
line run > Screen own

side entry left
side File(data/note.txt) between
side Screen right
